[d46e — the smeared interacting identification, with the g = 0 column]
  banner: GREEN-UNREVIEWED — the hostile round is deferred per the D46
  program pin (token budget); this receipt must not be cited as
  review-hardened until its round converts (paper-32's round precedes
  it).

  PRECISION AS RUN: exact truncated-series arithmetic (the d43a/d44d
  machinery, ported verbatim); mp.dps = 50 binary throughout the series
  layer; gate threshold 1e-30; commutator dust drop 1e-45 (d43a-ported);
  SG0 at ORD = 12 / L = 12 (the d44d SG0 code path); SG1/SG2/SG3 at
  ORD = 4 / DIM = 16 (the d44d KG3 phase, EXACT truncation: a Delta^p
  coefficient of series products/inverses depends only on input orders
  <= p).  SG4 re-runs the whole SG2/SG3 layer at mp.dps = 80 and gates
  every delivered constant to agree with the dps-50 run at 1e-30.
  FLOAT ENTRY POINTS (enumerated): (1) the series layer is mpmath binary
  at dps 50 / 80 — the fixture rationals (7/10, 1/2, 9/10, -2/5, 11/10,
  1/5) are rounded on entry, hence every gate is a 1e-30 threshold and
  never an mpf equality; (2) the recognition layer maps a dps-50 real to
  a Fraction by bounded-denominator best approximation (cap 1e15,
  accepted only at residual < 1e-30; census in SG4).  No others.
  Deterministic: no RNG, no wall clock, no hash-ordered output (every
  iteration is over an explicit list or a sorted key list; all dict keys
  are ints/int-tuples).  Rerun byte-identical (SG4).

  THE PIN'S QUESTION (note-d46e §1): at the free core BOTH admission
  rules collapse, under the corpus's continuum identification, onto the
  SAME tangential operator ray with rule-relative constants only.  At
  the interacting fixture the RAW singleton-bracket comparison DIVERGES
  — but D44d's round showed that divergence is GRAIN-INHERITED (present
  at g = 0 too).  Does the SMEARED (identified-operator) comparison
  collapse onto a common ray?  Every interacting cell below is printed
  beside its own g = 0 twin from the same pipeline.

  THE IDENTIFICATION AT THE INTERACTING FIXTURE (declared BEFORE any
  verdict).  The corpus construction is the tau FIRST MOMENT
    tau(delta, ch) = sum_{r in rs} r * sum_{entries in channel ch with
                     displacement delta} [A(b), A(b+r)]_{uv},
    D(ch) = sum_delta delta * tau(delta, ch)          (d43a/d44d/d45a),
  ported with the two free-core structures replaced by their fixture
  analogues, both declared here: (i) DISPLACEMENT — the free core reads
  delta off the site index of the matrix entry; on the occupation basis
  the analogue is the OCCUPATION DIPOLE displacement delta(u,v) =
  X(v) - X(u), X(u) = sum_n n*u_n (a hop across one bond shifts X by
  exactly 1, so this reduces to the free-core lattice displacement on
  the one-particle sector); (ii) CHANNEL — the free core's channel is
  the spinor pair (s, s') and the residual index i is SUMMED.  The
  occupation basis has no site/spin factorization, so a FAMILY of
  channel readings is pre-registered, coarse to fine, and EVERY one is
  reported:
    FULL — no summation at all (channel = the entry itself): the finest
           reading, grading-free.  A collapse here implies a collapse in
           every coarsening; a NON-collapse here does NOT imply one.
    ROW / COL — sum over the column / row partner at fixed row / column
           state (the 'dipole current' carried by each configuration).
    PAR  — channel = (X(u) mod 2, X(v) mod 2), the staggered-sublattice
           analogue of the free-core spinor pair: a 2x2 object directly
           comparable to the free-core ray form c*(I - sigma_x).
    SEC  — channel = the particle-number sector N (the block label of
           the D44d KG3 extraction gate).
  Cells: base b and separation set rs in {(b=0, rs=1,2,3), (b=0,
  rs=1,2), (b=1, rs=1,2)}; the last is the d44d KG3 pair set
  (R={1},S={2}) and (R={1},S={3}) exactly.  Regions are SINGLETONS.

  RAY VERDICT CLASSES (pre-registered; all are delivered outcomes at
  exit 0): COLLAPSE = D^LT = c * D^EXC over the whole channel set with
  ONE constant c (relative deviation < 1e-30) — the free-core outcome;
  STRUCTURED = proportional within every particle-number sector with
  per-sector constants but not globally; SUPPORT-MISMATCH = one rule's
  identified operator vanishes identically in that channel while the
  other does not (no common ray is even definable); BOTH-ZERO = both
  vanish; NO-COLLAPSE = neither.
  The reported constant c is read off a CANONICAL reference channel —
  the str-least channel attaining max |D^EXC| within relative 1e-25 —
  because exact ties for that maximum occur here and a bare argmax
  would make the printed number precision-dependent; the VERDICT CLASS
  is reference-free (proportionality does not depend on which channel
  normalizes it), and SG4-A gates the whole layer at dps 80.
  A NO-COLLAPSE is a finding, not a failure — but per the D44d §5 B1
  lesson it is meaningless without its
  g = 0 twin, which is why SG3 separates GRAIN (what the g = 0 twin
  already does) from the INTERACTION EFFECT (the computed difference).

  DECLARED PIN DEVIATIONS (owned in-receipt): (D1) the fixture is a
  4-site OPEN chain, so there is no translation average and no
  completeness slot beyond r = 3 — the r-range is the full available
  range at each base, and the three cells above are its full sweep;
  (D2) the channel-reading FAMILY above is this receipt's construction —
  the pin says 'the same tau first-moment construction', which fixes the
  moment but not the fixture's channel analogue, so all five readings
  are run and reported rather than one being privileged; (D3) ONE
  interacting point (pin §3) and ONE collar convention (d44d A6) — the
  three-convention robustness sweep is D44d's, not re-run here.

[SG0 — free-core regression through the ported pipeline (ORD 12, L 12)]
  [PASS] SG0-PF port fidelity: the region-collar builder == the singleton collar builder entrywise (lam = 1 and 1/2), exact
  [PASS] SG0-A the EXC singleton A(1) (d44d AN1): diag 1/2 at n0, 1/4 at n0+-1, -1/4 spin-flip off-diagonals, same-spin zero, columns sum zero  (exact at 1e-30)
  [PASS] SG0-B THE FREE-CORE RAY COLLAPSE re-run (d44d T5 / d45a YG1): both admission rules' identified operators land on the SAME ray (I - sigma_x) with rule-relative constants — EXC = 1, LT = kappa(m) with kappa(1/2) = 13/2304 and kappa(1) = -1/72 (sign flip); the committed signed tau channel tables reproduced; delta-odd in every channel of both rules; the d45a polynomial (9m^4 - 15m^2 + 4)/144 agrees at both anchors in EXACT Fraction arithmetic  (m=0.5: EXC D = 1*(I - sx) True; LT D = 13/2304*(I - sx) True; tau table True; delta-odd True; d45a poly True; m=1.0: EXC D = 1*(I - sx) True; LT D = -1/72*(I - sx) True; tau table True; delta-odd True; d45a poly True)
  [SG0 NOTE] this is the behaviour the interacting cells below are compared against: ONE ray, TWO rule-relative constants.

[SG1 — the interacting fixture, its extraction-validity gates, and the d44d KG3 re-anchor (ORD 4, DIM 16)]
  fixture (d44d KG3, ported): the root validator's minimal interacting
  gauge-matter occupation Hamiltonian, 4 sites, open chain, committed
  point (m, g) = (7/10, 1/2), t = 1, lambda = (9/10, -2/5, 11/10, 1/5);
  basis = the validator's particle_basis order (site 0 = MSB);
  H = sum_n m*(-1)^n n_n - g * sum_n lambda_n * prod_{s<=n}(-1)^{n_s}
      - t * sum_bonds hop.  Region collar (d44d A6): C_{n0} = the
  site's mass term + the electric term of INDEX n0 + the hopping bonds
  incident to n0; B = H - C.  The g = 0 twin is the SAME builder with
  the coupling set to zero — one code path, two columns.
  [PASS] SG1-A the interacting H is Hermitian (real symmetric) as built (d44d KG3-A)  (max dev 0.0)
  [PASS] SG1-B the g = 0 twin is the SAME fixture with the coupling removed: the two Hamiltonians differ ONLY on the diagonal (the electric gauge-string term) and differ there by a computed nonzero amount — the twin is neither a copy nor a different model  (max diagonal deviation = 13/10; max off-diagonal deviation = 0.0)
