  [PASS] SG3-C the EXC COLUMN IS COUPLING-BLIND, gated: the EXC leading (Delta^2) region coefficient is entrywise IDENTICAL at g = 1/2 and g = 0, hence so is every EXC identified operator in every reading. Mechanism (exact, order by order): Gamma = |U|^2, so at Delta^2 the off-diagonal entry is |H_ij|^2 and the diagonal entry is -sum_{k != i} |H_ik|^2 — the diagonal of H (which is where the electric gauge-string term and ONLY it lives in this fixture, SG1-B) cancels out of the modulus at this order. The interaction therefore enters the ray comparison ONLY through the LT side  (max coefficient deviation = 8.02e-51; max identified-operator deviation = 3.21e-50)
